## What `entity_id` can be:
- catalog ID → product sets in catalog, paginated (hidden/auto-generated excluded).
- set ID → that one set, one-row page, `name`/`limit`/`cursor` ignored.
- item ID → sets containing that product, paginated.

## Identifier types
See `catalog://id-conventions` via resources/read.

## When to use:
- Browse/search sets in catalog → pass `entity_id=<catalog_id>`, optionally with `name`.
- Inspect one set → pass `entity_id=<product_set_id>`.
- Find sets containing product → pass `entity_id=<product_id>`.

